{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":6,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1543066161,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDE1NDkwMzI4OQ=="},"target":"9b903eb684169ded0019b0ecaa291bff24e4853035bcf5eb6cf6655be9d0f020","message":"I need to conduct an analysis for which I need some files that are available on the web in a password-protected ZIP file. Alternatively, there is a Datalad dataset that references the files in the ZIP archive, but I do not have access to any of the remote with these file that the dataset knows about.\n\nWhen I use `datalad add-archive-content` on the ZIP file in annex it fails, because it doesn't have it an ddoesn't ask for the password. It actually asks, but datalad doesn't channel the request through to the terminal.\n@yarikoptic \n\nHere is a demo file (password is 'password'): [demo_encrypted.zip](https://github.com/datalad/datalad/files/2612172/demo_encrypted.zip)\n\n```\n(datalad3-dev) mih@meiner /tmp % datalad rev-create 2555\n[INFO   ] Creating a new annex repo at /tmp/2555 \n(dataset)                                                              \n(datalad3-dev) mih@meiner /tmp % cd 2555\n(datalad3-dev) mih@meiner /tmp/2555 (git)-[master] % git annex addurl https://github.com/datalad/datalad/files/2612172/demo_encrypted.zip\naddurl https://github.com/datalad/datalad/files/2612172/demo_encrypted.zip \n(to github.com_datalad_datalad_files_2612172_demo_encrypted.zip) ok\n(recording state in git...)\n(datalad3-dev) 1 mih@meiner /tmp/2555 (git)-[master] % datalad rev-save\nsave(ok): . (dataset)\n(datalad3-dev) mih@meiner /tmp/2555 (git)-[master] % datalad add-archive-content github.com_datalad_datalad_files_2612172_demo_encrypted.zip\n[INFO   ] Adding content of the archive github.com_datalad_datalad_files_2612172_demo_encrypted.zip into annex \u003cAnnexRepo path=/tmp/2555 (\u003cclass 'datalad.support.annexrepo.AnnexRepo'\u003e)\u003e \n[INFO   ] Initiating special remote datalad-archives \n\n\u003cHANGS INDEFINITELY until CTRL-C\u003e\n\n[ERROR  ] Command `['/usr/bin/7z', 'x', '-o/tmp/2555/.git/datalad/tmp/archives/2aac00bcd5', '--', '/tmp/2555/.git/annex/objects/zK/mF/MD5E-s372--b7cffd22d5c4e560726691cf87dfdf7f.zip/MD5E-s372--b7cffd22d5c4e560726691cf87dfdf7f.zip']' returned non-zero exit status 2 [util.py:run_checked:227] (PatoolError) \n```","files":null},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1527240103,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDE2NDYxODU2MDc="},"added":["question"],"removed":[]},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1527240286,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDE2NDYxOTE1NzY="},"added":["severity-normal"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1527240328,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM5MTk5NTk3OA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2555#issuecomment-391995978"},"message":"Also, after I Ctrl-C the command it leaves behind a folder tree like this:\n\n```\nb'\\\n   all\\\n      elements\\\n        of\\\n           the\\\n              absolute\\\n                 dataset\\\n                     path\\\n```\nand underneath empty files for all the archive content (which is a consequence of the passwd issue). This path, however, smells like a byte-string confusion. Running under PY3 with current master.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1527483819,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM5MjQxOTgzNg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2555#issuecomment-392419836"},"message":"Any thoughts @yarikoptic ?","files":null},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1543053765,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE0OlVubGFiZWxlZEV2ZW50MTk4NDkzODkwMQ=="},"added":[],"removed":["question"]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1543054501,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ0MTM1NzEyNg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2555#issuecomment-441357126"},"message":"Added a demo file and output to top message.","files":null},{"type":6,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1543054501,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDE1NDg4NzgzOQ=="},"target":"d92731b6579951c45a09e7802278f4ccab9fe047707044e02c476568615ca381","message":"Added a demo file and output to top message. The byte-string issue is no longer present.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1543064542,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ0MTM2NjQzMw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2555#issuecomment-441366433"},"message":"I feel that it is patool which doesn't really support it. I would look first into making sure patool could deal with that prompt and/or through some dedicated exception that archive needs a password so extraction could be responding with the password. Then we could ask user they password and provide it into extract call","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1543066770,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ0MTM2ODYwNQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2555#issuecomment-441368605"},"message":"So you are saying patool needs to be replaced by a proper tool? What were the reasons for selecting patool in the first place -- does anyone know? Speaks anything against stdlib `zipfile`?\n\nRegardless of the underlying tools, it seems that `add-archive-content` needs an API change to be able to accept a password.\n\nBut even that won't be enough. If `get` needs to obtain that archive in order to get a file from it, this layer of code also needs to be able to prompt for a password, and/or get it from somewhere.\n\nOn the topic of patool itself: I can confirm that a\n\n```\npatoolib.extract_archive('demo_encrypted.zip', outdir='.', interactive=True)\npatool: Extracting demo_encrypted.zip ...\npatool: running /usr/bin/7z x -o. -- demo_encrypted.zip\n```\n\njust hangs until it is killed. When I run the displayed 7z command, it prompts for a password as expected. I thought to report a bug, but then found https://github.com/wummel/patool/issues/20 which labels the extraction of a single specified file as an edge case that will not be supported -- and decided against it.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1543069142,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ0MTM3MTIwOQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2555#issuecomment-441371209"},"message":"I was saying that the fix might need to be done in patool first.  I never suggested replacement or stated that patool is \"not proper\".  Oh this \"media coverage\" ppl ;-)\nHaving said that - sticking to \"standard\" libraries would be beneficial. `zipfile` probably has much narrow coverage of archivers, we would probably also need `tarfile`, etc, and provide uniform interface to them, and even then some would be supported only by patool. So, we could may be try zipfile as the first option, and if fails - try with patool?  While at it would be worthwhile checking support for large (\u003e4GB) .zip files and extraction from series of split archives.\n\n`get` -- I believe password (if you use our `ui`) would work even when sandwiched from the special remote, that is how we request credentials in such as cases as well.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1579432252,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU3NTk5MzcyMw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2555#issuecomment-575993723"},"message":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/pull/4041 has an alternative implementation based on `7z`. `7z` provides a `-p` parameter with which passwords for protected archives can be set on compression and decompression -- for any archive type that supports it (like ZIP).","files":null}]}